-- title:
--   Integral right ideals split off a power of the ramified prime
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $q'$ be a prime number. Assume `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q'`, i.e. $a<0$, $b<0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ the ring $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division ring (every nonzero element is a unit) precisely when $q'$ lies in $v$. Let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is a maximal order, that is: $1\in\Lambda$, $\Lambda$ is closed under multiplication, $\Lambda$ spans $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, $\Lambda$ is finitely generated, and every submodule with these four properties containing $\Lambda$ equals $\Lambda$. Let $x$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ (finite adèles of $\mathbb{Q}$), and write $\Lambda(x):=$ [`Submodule.ofFiniteIdele Λ x`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L19) for the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of those $h\in\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ whose image $h\otimes 1$ lies in $x\cdot$[`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox Λ`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14), the latter being the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $\alpha$ a finite adèle integral at every place. Assume $\Lambda(x)\le\Lambda$. Then there exist $k\in\mathbb{N}$ and a unit $x_0$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ such that $\Lambda(x_0)\le\Lambda$, such that $\Lambda(x_0)$ contains some $h\neq 0$ with $v_{q'}(\mathrm{nrd}\,h)=0$, where $\mathrm{nrd}\,h=h_{\mathrm{re}}^2-a\,h_I^2-b\,h_J^2+ab\,h_K^2$, and such that, as subsets of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, $$\Lambda(x)=\Lambda(x_0)\cap\{h\mid h\in\Lambda \text{ and } (h=0 \text{ or } k\le v_{q'}(\mathrm{nrd}\,h))\}.$$
--
--   This records the local structure at the ramified prime of an integral right ideal of a maximal order in a definite rational quaternion algebra ramified exactly at $q'$: the ideal is the intersection of a part prime to $q'$ (an ideal containing an element of reduced norm a $q'$-adic unit) with the $k$-th power of the unique maximal two-sided ideal above $q'$, the latter described as the set of elements of $\Lambda$ whose reduced norm has $q'$-adic valuation at least $k$. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, by [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_kernelIdealSet_eq_star_smul_ofFiniteIdele`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_kernelIdealSet_eq_star_smul_ofFiniteIdele).
